  "summary": "Finland completed Onkalo, the world's first permanent nuclear repository carved 450m into bedrock, designed to seal radioactive waste for 100,000 years without human intervention. Hook: 'A tomb built to stay untouched for 100,000 years.'",
  "notes": "- Onkalo repository located on Olkiluoto Island in western Finland.\n- Tunnels bored 450 meters deep into 1.9-billion-year-old stable crystalline granite bedrock.\n- Copper canisters wrapped in bentonite clay buffer to withstand future ice ages and tectonic shifts.\n- Intentionally designed without warning markers so future human civilizations aren't tempted to dig it up.",
  "analyzed_at": "2026-11-04T03:22:23Z"
